\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 10. Middleware preview\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Middleware sits between steps so you can intervene:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Before a tool call: authenticate, validate, block the call if checks fail\
\ls14\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 After a tool call: log the output, strip sensitive data, audit\
\ls14\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 On the AI message: block profanity, prevent system prompt leakage\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Also useful for debugging, analytics, and guardrails. Full coverage comes later, but understanding message types now is what makes middleware logic possible.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 11. Q&A worth keeping\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Multi-agent routing.
\f1\b0  With several specialised agents, do not send every agent's full MD instruction file to the router. Store a short name + one-paragraph description per agent (an agent registry) and route on that, roughly 300 tokens per agent. This mirrors how Claude Skills work: only the name and description get loaded, never the whole file. Agents must be distinct from each other for routing to work.\

\f0\b Cross-user knowledge reuse.
\f1\b0  If one user's answer is useful to another, that is long-term memory territory (Mem0 and similar), not fine-tuning. The agent queries memory before hitting the model. Covered later in the course.\

\f0\b Function calling vs tool calling vs MCP.
\f1\b0  A function is the base unit. A tool is a function wrapped so the AI can use it. MCP is a collection of tools. A2A (agent-to-agent) is a separate concept from agent-as-a-tool.\

\f0\b Async.
\f1\b0  
\f4\fs26 asyncio
\f1\fs24  is the base library and is enough. 
\f4\fs26 aiohttp
\f1\fs24  for web requests.\

\f0\b MCP tools returning huge payloads.
\f1\b0  Scraping tools can return gigabytes. Filter and store locally, then feed only the relevant slice into the context window.\

\f0\b Skills vs system message vs tools.
\f1\b0  Skill = step-by-step instructions for a specific task. It can reference tools but cannot connect them. System message = the agent's general personality and rules. Tool = an actual callable function.\

\f0\b Guardrails.
\f1\b0  Both DIY and framework options exist (Guardrails AI, plus LangChain's own facilities). Purpose: control what the AI outputs and prevent data leakage in production.\

\f0\b Evaluation and observability.
\f1\b0  Opik, LangSmith, Langfuse, Phoenix. To be covered separately near the end so it does not distract from building.\

\f0\b Authentication.
\f1\b0  Nothing special. Key-based auth to the model, ordinary Python auth for tools, secrets via GitHub Secrets or AWS Secrets Manager. Middleware can enforce checks before a sensitive tool runs.\

\f0\b PDF extraction into a vector DB.
\f1\b0  For structure-aware extraction (position, titles, page furniture), look at 
\f0\b Docling
\f1\b0 .\

\f0\b OpenAI billing.
\f1\b0  $5 with auto-reload switched off is enough for the learning phase. Projects will need more.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

